<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss version="2.0"><channel><title>Ngrok incidents — Vendor Status Watch</title><link>https://approjects-vendor-status-watch.static.hf.space/v/ngrok.html</link><description>Incidents from Ngrok's public status page, polled daily.</description><lastBuildDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 05:19:27 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>New accounts or newly created authtokens are not able to connect [resolved]</title><link>https://stspg.io/bvhnjx5zffsq</link><guid isPermaLink="false">ngrok:2026-09-03T23:34:59.000Z</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 23:34:59 +0000</pubDate><description>This incident has been resolved.</description></item><item><title>User invites disruption [resolved]</title><link>https://stspg.io/gss8dg777mv5</link><guid isPermaLink="false">ngrok:2026-08-28T16:00:00.000Z</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>Between August 28 and September 1, people invited to an ngrok account couldn&#x27;t accept the invitation. The invitation link returned an error instead of signing the user in. An authentication change shipped on August 28 broke the URL that redeems an invitation. We moved redemption to login.ngrok.com, and invitations worked again from September 1 at 00:21 UTC. Users routed through Tokyo kept seeing the error until 14:15 UTC, when we cleared a stale routing config in that region. If an invitation still fails, ask the account owner to send a new one, or email support@ngrok.com.</description></item><item><title>Delays issuing certificates [resolved]</title><link>https://stspg.io/mfc4m9lmryc9</link><guid isPermaLink="false">ngrok:2026-06-18T20:16:08.183Z</guid><pubDate>Thu, 18 Jun 2026 20:16:08 +0000</pubDate><description>This incident has been resolved.</description></item><item><title>SSO Login to the ngrok Dashboard is currently redirecting back to the login page [resolved]</title><link>https://stspg.io/mkk67vwccb9f</link><guid isPermaLink="false">ngrok:2026-05-15T00:49:55.754Z</guid><pubDate>Fri, 1